From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe14 <engine@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:59:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] core, frontend: Fire Emblem Fates' randomizer for Seal
 of Flames too

The owner asked that the randomizer work for every path and story, Seal of
Flames included (F-047, round 58). Seal of Flames by Laz14
(gamebanana.com/mods/656034, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) shares Fates' title id
(0004000000179800) and plays from its own profile with its files laid over
the game's RomFS (Zakuro's mods folder).

- Config gets fates_rando_game: None (the default, every existing caller and
  Fire Emblem Fates) or Some("seal"). The frontend now leaves fates_rando on
  for both games and sets fates_rando_game from game_pick::rando_game(choice);
  the Esc menu's Randomizer entry and the page's schema ask are no longer
  held back for Seal of Flames.
- make_run_for: for Seal the tool command gets two more arguments, the game
  and <data>/mods/<title>/romfs (mod_romfs, Zakuro's upper/lower-case title
  folder rule); the Python snippet then calls tools/randomizer/sources.py
  activate first, so the run is made from the mod's own tables and its patch
  guards are the mod's bytes. For Fates the command is the same as before.
- answer_for: a Seal answer gets "game": "seal" first, so its runs have their
  own ids and their options.json names the game. A Fates answer is unchanged.
- Placement files: Seal reads its RomFS through zakuro_fs::layered::Layered.
  Layered::lookup(path) gives a file's (data offset, size) in the layered
  image; placements() uses it when fates_rando_game is set (Fates with a
  layered RomFS still gets none, as before), make_placement reads the stored
  file through Layered::read, and read_file's Layered branch calls
  overlay_read like the plain RomImage branch.

Every cell is still checked against its original value before anything is
written (all or nothing): a Seal run on the original game's tables (or the
reverse) is refused whole at GameData, so nothing is laid.

Checked: cargo test -p zakuro-core --lib, -p zakuro-fs --lib, -p zakuro --lib
all pass (new: answer_for and run ids, mod_romfs, the make snippet,
Layered::lookup against Layered::read, game_pick::rando_game).
